WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.360
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.030
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.040
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.710
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.170
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.060
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.390
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.940
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.150
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.410
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.540
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.830
Won't go away

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.710
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.760
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.720
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.780
It's amazing!

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.040
We can never find the sea like this in Japan.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.830
It's blue everywhere.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.210
Dad!

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.720
Dad, aren't you going to swim?

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.730
That's a battleship... A battleship, isn't it?

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.900
Wow, I wonder which country it belongs to?

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.740
- It's a Japanese cruiser.
- Japanese?

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.570
Yes, a long time ago, the Japanese were at war...

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.950
Even these beautiful South Sea islands were battlegrounds.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.760
Maritime Self-Defense Force
Officers' Training School

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.590
The Yukinami model is developed from the Kongo-class vessel,

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.010
the first Aegis-class defense ship in Japan.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.470
Its distinctive feature is the addition of a helicopter hangar

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.970
at the ship's stern.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:31.690
The Mirai, on which I serve as Executive Officer, is a Yukinami class No. 3.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.310
- The stealth performance...
- Yosuke...

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.820
...is pretty eloquent in his speech.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.190
That's just one of his jobs.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.740
An advanced system has been added to the Aegis system of the ship.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:49.330
It used to be impossible to jam communication transmissions.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.080
Though limited to short range, such jamming is now possible.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.580
In principle, we do that by...

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.250
His speech sounds pretty tense.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.840
I guess he's really nervous.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.840
The calm Kikuchi that we know?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.590
Well, Masayuki is occasionally timid, you know?

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.890
In conclusion, fleet mobilization brings out the Aegis ship's full potential.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.230
It's all about team work!

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.520
Just like the Botaoshi game in the National Defense Academy, during my...

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.070
What is he here to talk about?

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.070
No idea.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.320
The Aegis escort ship is well-known for its high-tech capabilities.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.740
However, as represented by the name Aegis,

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.870
which literally means "God's Shield",

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.460
its true duty is to protect not only convoy ships, but also our country itself.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.330
Soon you will all graduate from here,

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.380
and will become successful in the units you go on to.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:43.380
Please consider once again the abilities that all of you possess.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.470
- That's all.
- Attention!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.720
Salute.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.730
Headmaster Present

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:55.230
I'm sorry that you guys had to do more than just the greeting.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.730
Not at all, it's an honour to think that my speech might help.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.150
It's already been 12 years since you were commissioned.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.620
Three classmates assigned to be officers of the same ship,

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.870
I think it's the first time this has happened.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.080
I guess the plan is to put together a team of the elite.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.750
But it would never have happened without you, sir.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:22.590
Well, it means this mission must be very important.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.550
I have high expectations for the three of you.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.850
I wasn't on the student board like you, Yosuke,

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.140
and I wasn't an honors student like Masayuki, either.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.480
But for someone like me to be giving a speech...

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.060
Well...

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:42.070
I chose the National Defense Academy due to economical reasons.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.650
Someone like Kohei, who'd aspired to join Marine Defense,

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.360
...would be much more suitable, I guess.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.490
Aspired? I don't know about that.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:56.660
I just got bored with fighting small skirmishes to protect the flag.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.170
I'd prefer to do something on the bigger scale.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.630
Protecting Japan... that's something bigger.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.840
It is indeed.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.130
But don't be picking any fights.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:11.180
I think I was influenced by my father.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.600
Yeah, Yosuke's father was...

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:16.390
...one of the first graduates from the National Defense Academy.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.350
That's right. Dad was really searching for something...

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.990
A long time ago, the Japanese were at war...

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.570
Even these beautiful South Sea islands were battlegrounds.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:35.080
I remember learning about it in my Social Studies class.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:38.620
Everybody suffered because of the war.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:42.500
It's wrong to have a war, right?

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.960
Those soldiers took the enemies' lives whether or not they wanted to.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.180
They'd have died if they hadn't done so.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.390
They fought to protect Japan, their country...

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.850
their homeland and their beloved families,

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.180
risking their own lives.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.350
Well then, who are the bad guys?

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.310
What were they?

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.900
I'd like to know the answers, too.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.410
After all...

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.830
In the end, like my father,

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.830
I've been searching for answers to justify my own queries.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.500
Will you look at that, it's still here.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.550
Yamato-class 46 cm armor piercing shell.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:29.720
Model type 91.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:35.550
Shot at 45 degrees, it'll reach a distance of 42km in 90 seconds.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.930
- Makes me shiver.
- Don't forget,

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:42.810
with the Mirai's Aegis system, we can intercept the launched rounds.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.230
Indeed.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.820
But no matter how good the system is,

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.320
it really comes down to the person operating it.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.780
If Kikuchi is the Weapons Officer, we'll never miss.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.660
Well, well, what strong trust you have.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.870
But I have to say, I agree.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.970
Nothing here has changed. The atmosphere's still the same.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.390
Yeah, my purpose wasn't to meet with him or give a speech.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.900
I just wanted to see this place again.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.810
Same here.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.780
We're thinking the same thing, aren't we?

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:34.110
Inside there, are the heirs of deceased Admiral Nelson of the Royal navy,

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.070
as well as Admiral Heihachiro Togo,

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:41.830
and Combined Fleet Commander in Chief Admiral Isoroku Yamamoto.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.210
But nobody has actually seen them, right?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.460
You don't have to show them if it isn't necessary.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.920
More importantly, the people must believe they are there.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:55.090
This applies to the principle of protecting the country, I suppose.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:22.200
Kohei, are you sure you don't need to visit your grandmother and Tomoko?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.660
Yeah, my grandmother's still in good health. I can visit her anytime.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.460
I see.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.340
Etajima is our starting point.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:33.050
We can start afresh whenever we come back here.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:37.090
Thank you, Etajima. We'll be back soon.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:42.900
Yokosuka Station

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.130
Captain Umezu!

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:20.180
Commander Kadomatsu, Kikuchi and Oguri reporting.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.600
Welcome back.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.140
Is there a problem with the ship?

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:28.890
No, I was just taking a good look at it.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:31.060
It's a habit of mine before departure.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.780
There's nothing for me to do the day before we pull out, anyway.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.450
By the way, I have a favor to ask of you.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.360
What is it, Sir?

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.870
Oh, a newspaper reporter would like to interview us.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:46.330
I'm not very good with handling the media.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.460
I am not very good at handling them either, sir.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:54.000
Well, you're doing your Captain a favor. Please take care of it.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.510
All hands on deck in 5 minutes.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.640
Is our captain going to be like that even after we set sail?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.930
I guess that's why people say he's "a person who doesn't stand out."

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.810
Navigation Officer, Weapons Officer.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:10.640
I will not tolerate any criticism of our captain once we are on board.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:13.190
It might have a demoralizing effect on our crew.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.190
- I sincerely apologize.
- I'll be more careful.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.650
I am Katagiri, a free journalist.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.120
Executive Officer, I have been waiting for you.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.240
Can I chat with you for a bit?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:29.580
We are busy preparing to embark. It'd be great if you could wait till tonight.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.620
No problem.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:35.090
I'll kill some time by taking pictures onboard.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.520
Your father was in the marine,

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.360
so you've decided to follow his footsteps...

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:59.280
...and joined the Defense Academy?

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.530
That's it?

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.700
Should there be anything more?

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:06.450
What about a desire to protect the country,

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.790
or your concerns over the future of the SDF,

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:11.040
or something more catchy, you know?

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:14.830
As a military man, I only know about ships.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.540
Then, what about this?

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.630
Tomorrow, this Aegis-class ship, Mirai, and other escort vessels,

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:24.340
will be pulling out of port on their first large-scale training drill.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.810
It is just a drill this time, but in the future,

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.430
if they are to face a real fighting situation,

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:34.480
will the JSDF be able to handle it?

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:39.650
Mr. Katagiri. Have you ever killed somebody?

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:41.530
What? No.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.990
We're no different from you journalists, Mr. Katagiri.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:49.490
Nobody has experienced a real war and we never want to have one.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.450
The only difference between you and I is...

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.460
I am wearing this uniform.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.380
If there is an order, we have to obey.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.010
Your time is up. If you'll excuse me.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:07.470
Commander Kadomatsu, that might be an appropriate comment,

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.890
but is that your personal opinion as well?

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.560
- Take in line 6.
- Prepare to get underway.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:18.440
The Maritime Self-Defense Force will participate in the joint drill run

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.150
with the US military in the South Pacific.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:22.610
Take in line 3.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.240
Take in remaining lines.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.330
Slow ahead two.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.290
Slow ahead two!

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.960
Prepare to salute the Commanding Officer.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.130
Salute Commanding Officer.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.130
Attention! To port.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.100
Present!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.850
All hands, present head gear.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.990
Let's take her half ahead two.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:14.830
The dispatched ships are: the Destroyer Aoba,

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.870
the two Aegis ships, Haruka and Mirai,

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.710
and the supply ship Amagi, a total of four.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.630
The ships are now leaving...

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:29.130
...to join the US Naval Fleet in the open waters off Hawaii.

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:34.980
The Mirai Sets Sail

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:42.490
Fourth Day of Voyage
Longitude:  153 degrees East
Latitude:    25 degrees North
Off Minamitorishima Island

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.620
EMS detection, 120 degrees.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.040
Prepare an anti-aircraft drill.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.710
Port engine ahead. Full.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.260
The missile seeker has been locked on to us.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.050
- Take it calm.
- Yes, sir.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:13.140
Prepare to launch Sea Sparrow. Illuminator is linked.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.850
Target will be in range in 4 seconds.

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:19.270
3, 2, 1. Target in range.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:20.850
Fire!

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:24.440
First target hit. Second target approaching.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.980
Nicely done, Weapons Officer.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.570
"CIWS: Close-In Weapons System"

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.570
CIWS, prepare to intercept incoming ordinance. Begin EA.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:31.820
Brace for impact. Port Side.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.080
CIWS, start firing with AAW automatic mode.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.080
"AAW: Anti-Air Warfare"

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.910
Missile inbound, port side at 90 degrees.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.380
Impact to port side main hull.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.710
Petty Officer Yanagi is injured.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.460
Me?

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:50.590
Flooding at bulkhead 32 Port side!

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:55.350
Move it! The ship and her crew are depending on us!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.890
If you do this slowly, we're going down!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:07.570
The sky... looks really strange.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:10.030
We've concluded the drill, Captain.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.570
Roger.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.490
We're behind our target by five minutes, sir.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.070
That's acceptable for now.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.280
Compared to a month ago, when the delay was ten minutes,

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:18.870
that's a 5 minute improvement.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:19.790
Yes, sir.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.920
Don't be too eager, or you won't last very long.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:25.250
Don't strain yourself too much.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.920
By the way, Navigator,

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:29.840
can you receive the weather information?

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.300
Yes, Sir.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:37.510
Captain. We have received a report from the Meteorological Agency.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.020
There's a low pressure front, northeast of the Midway Islands.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.810
Pressure is at 965 hectopascal,

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:46.520
wind speed at 40 knots, and gaining.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.440
This wasn't in the forecast.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:51.400
Looks like we got a storm coming. Prep the ship for rough weather.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:52.650
Yes, Sir.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:56.370
Move within 4000 yards of the other ships. Maintain close contact.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:17:00.160
Storm preparation. Approach the gunwale.

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:17.680
This isn't a drill. This one's real!

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.680
It's been over 30 years since I first stepped out onto the sea.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.060
I've never seen a sky quite like this.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.240
What is it? Lightning strike?

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:38.780
Emergency Command Center, I need a damage report right now!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:43.830
All electrical systems are online. No abnormalities registered.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.380
Bridge to CIC.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:53.550
We're not detecting the other ships on radar. We've lost them.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.630
How could all radar just fail?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:56.510
Communication status?

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:59.640
Can't establish communication with the Haruka.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.260
No trace of Aoba and Amagi as well.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:05.430
Nothing on all frequencies!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:09.650
Haruka was 4000 yards ahead of us just 5 minutes ago.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.400
How about the satellite?

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.400
We can't capture the geostationary satellite.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:16.150
Check the tracking antenna.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.410
It's not broken.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.990
But there's no response from all the other ships.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:25.290
What on earth is happening?

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.960
Do a full search to locate the lost consort ships.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.040
They couldn't have sunk all of a sudden.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.250
Yes, Sir!

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:41.470
Navigator, what is that?

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.020
This can't be... In open sea near Hawaii?

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:48.890
But, this is no doubt an aurora!

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.580
We're getting abnormal readings on all instruments.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.750
They are out of control!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:16.130
We might have gotten into a strong magnetic storm.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:18.090
What's the word from CIC?

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.630
Bridge to CIC, I need that status report now.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:25.640
All detection systems and control are inoperative.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.560
There's excessive noise in the phone, and we can't hear clearly.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.890
This ship is the newest type.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.850
This shouldn't be happening!

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:43.030
W-What? What is happening?

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:46.160
This ship had better be safe.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:02.430
All instruments and communication equipment are back online.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:04.850
Seems like we made it through.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.680
Check for any damage, quickly.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:08.010
Yes, sir!

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.310
Wh-What?

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:19.070
There are approximately 40 ships in the water around us!

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:21.030
We are in the middle of a large fleet!

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:25.320
The US fleet from Pearl Harbour has probably arrived ahead of schedule.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.950
Log in and get confirmation.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.040
Use the appropriate radio frequency to confirm.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:35.420
"SIF: Signal Identification Frequency"

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:35.420
No response on SIF from them.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.540
Target is approaching!

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:39.800
2500 yards from our bow!

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.800
The target is a large battleship!

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.790
Is it the <i>New Jersey</i>?  Or the <i>Iowa</i>?

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:14.750
All the Iowa class ships have been decommissioned.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.500
None of them would be out here in the Pacific.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.840
Then, what is it?

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.260
- Starboard engines, ahead full.
- Starboard engines, ahead full.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:28.220
Captain, isn't this...

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.430
Are my eyes playing tricks on me?

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:56.790
A long time ago, the Japanese were at war...

00:21:56.790 --> 00:22:00.210
Even these beautiful South Sea islands were battlegrounds.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:07.930
The battleship... Yamato?!

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:17.840
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:23.040
Just peacefully

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:34.850
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:47.730
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:54.370
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.940 --> 00:23:00.450
I kept on praying

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:12.260
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:14.130 --> 00:23:27.940
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:44.600
The Combined Fleet didn't appear in front of us.

00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:49.100
I think we've appeared... in the midst of the Battle of Midway.

00:23:49.140 --> 00:23:52.150
If this ship has really traveled through time,

00:23:52.440 --> 00:23:55.980
then what's waiting for us ahead... is a battlefield.

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:58.700
Look, it's a war out there!

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:00.160
And this is a war ship.

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:03.990
What better way to test a warship than to go to war!

00:24:00.490 --> 00:24:05.460
Next Episode: Midway

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:10.460
